sequenceDiagram
    accTitle: Multi-turn query agent — what a follow-up remembers and does
    accDescr: The streaming browser conversation carries history between fresh server turns. A first data question uses MCP to generate and execute SQL. Later turns can explain retained results, ask for clarification, or query again with earlier intent. History holds complete user/assistant pairs with SQL, explanation, metadata, and all loaded rows. oldest pairs are removed to meet 40-message and 120,000-character limits. MCP is shared infrastructure, not persistent conversation memory. Direct-answer and clarification decisions are prompt-guided.
    %% Read next: 14-mcp-tool-lifecycle.mmd and 15-agent-safety-and-limits.mmd
    autonumber
    actor U as You
    participant B as Browser + history
    participant A as Fresh agent turn
    participant M as MCP query tools

    rect rgb(239, 246, 255)
        U->>B: Turn 1: Show the top 5 customers by balance
        B->>A: Question + retained history over WebSocket
        A->>A: Validate history. create a new request ID and context
        A->>M: construct_sql, then execute_query with its exact SQL
        M-->>A: Validated SQL + executed rows and metadata
        A->>M: summarize_results using all loaded rows
        M-->>A: Explanation of the current result
        A-->>B: Final answer + SQL + table + warnings
        Note over A,M: Release this request context in finally. the shared MCP connection stays available
        B->>B: Save a user/assistant pair: question, explanation, SQL, columns, rows, count, truncated flag
    end

    rect rgb(245, 243, 255)
        U->>B: Turn 2: Ask a follow-up
        B->>A: New question + retained complete pairs
        Note over B,A: Fresh turn state. continuity comes from supplied history, not the old request ID
        A->>A: Use history to decide what this question needs
        alt Earlier results support the answer: Explain that ranking
            A-->>B: Direct explanation. no tool call
        else Still ambiguous: Show the best ones
            A-->>B: Ask what best means. no tool call
        else New facts or changed SQL: Only active customers. refresh the ranking
            A->>M: construct_sql with earlier ranking intent + new filter
            M-->>A: Newly generated and validated SQL
            A->>M: execute_query, then optional server-run summary
            M-->>A: Fresh result + explanation
            A-->>B: Updated answer + SQL + table + warnings
        end
        Note over A,M: Each completed turn releases its request context, including direct answers
    end

    B->>B: After success, append the pair. remove oldest whole pairs until history fits
    Note over B,A: At most 40 messages / 120,000 characters. Keep all rows in each retained pair. even the newest pair can be dropped if too large
    Note over U,B: New chat clears browser history. Failed or cancelled turns are not appended
    Note over A,M: Earlier rows are a snapshot of that query, with its filters and limits. Unseen rows or fresh facts require a new query
